# Environments. 1.2 GB between the two, and both rebuild from
# requirements.txt (GPU) and requirements-analysis.txt (laptop).
.venv/
.venv-gpu/

# Street View imagery is not redistributable. Google's terms cap caching at
# 30 days; derived profiles and metrics are ours to publish, the JPEGs are
# scratch. 199 MB, and uploading them would be a licence breach as well as
# a repo nobody can clone.
data/raw/svi/

# The same photographs, one step removed: the per-face panels draw Street
# View pixels under the overlay, and the dashboard embeds those panels as
# base64. Both are regenerated by make_dashboard.py and tools/face_samples.py
# from data that is on disk locally.
results/figures/face_samples/
results/dashboard.html

# Credentials. GMAPS_KEY lives here and must never leave the machine.
.env

# Local safety copies of artefacts that cannot be regenerated cheaply.
# Keep them on disk; they are not history.
*.bak

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.claude/

# Street View imagery under any frame version. Google caps caching at 30 days
# and the JPEGs are not redistributable; only derived profiles are.
data/raw/svi_v12/
data/raw/svi_*/

# Superseded frames and scratch profile arrays. Kept on disk so a v12 result
# stays reproducible, but they are large binaries and not the current state.
data/processed/v12_*
data/processed/*.BACKUP-*.npz
data/processed/*.prev.npz
data/processed/azimuth_profiles_subset.npz
data/raw/v12_metadata.csv

# Derived report, regenerated by tools/build_sim_report.py in seconds.
results/sim_report.html

# SegFormer panels draw Street View pixels beside the mask, same licence
# problem as results/figures/face_samples/. The mask PNGs are derived, but
# they sit in the same directory and regenerate in minutes from the CSV run.
# results/tables/svi_180_segformer.csv is the derived metric and is kept.
results/svi_180_seg/

# Photo-over-mask comparison tree: Street View pixels again, and it rebuilds
# from results/svi_180_seg in seconds with tools/svi_180_comparison.py.
results/svi_180_segmented_comparison/

# Walk videos built from the comparison frames: Street View pixels once more,
# and tools/svi_180_walk_video.py rebuilds them from what is already on disk.
results/svi_180_walk_videos/

# Frozen-backbone embeddings for the label probe: a large binary that
# regenerates from the panoramas with tools/svi_180_probe_features.py.
data/processed/svi_180_dinov2.npz

# Qwen panels: photo, mask and ratings composited together -- Street View
# pixels again. results/tables/svi_180_qwen_morphology.csv holds the ratings.
results/svi_180_seg_comparison_QWEN2-VL_7B/

# --- Street View pixels in sheet form. Same rule as data/raw/svi_*: these
# are the exported panoramas at thumbnail size, so publishing them publishes
# Google's imagery. All three rebuild from data/raw/svi_180 in minutes.
results/review_sheets/
results/contact_sheets/
results/figures/sim_samples/

# --- Mask-only renders. Derived data and safe to publish, but 113 MB that
# regenerates in minutes from results/svi_180_seg. Attach to a Release rather
# than carrying it in every clone forever.
results/svi_180_masks_only/
results/svi_180_masks_only_videos/

# --- Third-party caches and re-downloadable inputs. None of it is ours and
# all of it refetches: contextily basemap tiles, OSM extracts, NYC open data,
# and the request cache.
data/processed/tiles/
data/processed/osm_cache/
data/processed/nyc_gis/
cache/

# --- Scratch profile array from the SIM grouping, 8.6 MB, same category as
# the other npz files above.
data/processed/sim_profiles.npz

# --- Regenerated by tools/export_gis.py from the layers the figures draw.
results/gis/

# Walk videos and GIFs built straight from the raw panoramas: unmodified
# Street View pixels, so the 30-day cache cap applies to these as much as to
# data/raw/svi_180. tools/svi_180_walk_video.py --src data/raw/svi_180 --gif
# rebuilds them in minutes from what is already on disk.
results/svi_180_streetview_walks/

# --- Run logs from the long GPU jobs. converge.err alone is 150 KB of tqdm
# carriage returns, and none of it is a result: the numbers that matter were
# written to results/tables. Keep them on disk while a run is being debugged.
*.log
*.err

# --- Pre-change safety copies. Same category as *.bak above, different
# extensions: azimuth_profiles.backup.npz predates the s05 geometry fix and
# metrics.csv.pre_cone / .pre_s05 predate the stages named in their suffix.
# They exist so a bad edit is recoverable, not so it is in history twice.
data/processed/*.backup.npz
data/processed/metrics.csv.pre_*
results/tables/*_backup_*.csv

# --- Scratch list of sample overlay paths, written while picking renders to
# look at. Regenerates with a find, and every path in it points into
# data/raw/svi_90_seg, which is ignored anyway.
picks.txt

# --- Superseded imagery trees. Rebuilt by their exporters in a minute or two,
# and covered by data/raw/svi_*/ above in any case: svi_180_old is the 627-node
# export before the tunnel heuristic was dropped, svi_180_hi a 2880 px width
# test of whether resolution explains the 90/180 share gap.
data/raw/svi_180_old/
data/raw/svi_180_hi/

# Claude Code's own working notes. Local to the machine and never committed:
# the copy that used to live here documented the v11 GVI/VEI study, went stale
# as the work moved to the SIM pipeline, and was then read back as if it were
# the method -- its capture-date note was used to justify discarding three
# quarters of the London frame. Removed from every branch in 449ed00 and
# adeb9ad. README.md and the module docstrings are the committed documentation.
CLAUDE.md

# ---- London imagery, same licence as Murray Hill's -------------------------
# data/raw/svi_*/ above covers the Manhattan frame only; London renders live
# under its own study-area root and were NOT matched, so a git add -A would
# have published 13,646 Street View JPEGs. The derived metrics are ours to
# publish and the photographs are not.
data/london/raw/

# ---- the walk-through pages ------------------------------------------------
# Self-contained by design: every frame is inlined as base64, so these are the
# imagery, 40 MB of it, wearing an .html extension. They are built locally and
# handed to the author's own machine; they must not be uploaded.
results/figures/walk_*.html

# GIFs and contact sheets of the walks: Street View pixels, unmodified
results/figures/walks/

# ---- figures that draw the photographs rather than the numbers -------------
# Plots of metrics are kept. These paste the imagery beside the mask or the
# label, which is the same redistribution by another route.
#
# PATH-AGNOSTIC ON PURPOSE. The first version of these rules said
# results/figures/..., which is the Manhattan frame's output root -- London
# writes to results/london/figures/ and matched none of them, leaving 129 MB
# of walk GIFs and segmentation panels staged to publish. A second study area
# must not be able to reintroduce the problem by having a different path.
**/figures/walks/
**/seg_examples_*.png
**/seg_london.png
**/seg_combined_*.png
**/seg_masks_*.png
**/mast_*_halves.png
**/label_batch_*.jpg
**/user_kept_*.jpg
**/london_covered_*.jpg
**/london_covered_*.png
**/london_indoor_flagged.png
**/walk_*.html

# run logs: machine paths and timings, no value to a reader
logs/

# ---- figures, and what exists only to draw them ----------------------------
# Every figure regenerates from the tables and the tools, so the repository
# carries the method and the numbers rather than the renders. That also
# removes a standing hazard: the panels that paste Street View pixels beside a
# mask lived in the same folders as the plots, and each new study area added
# its own copy under a path the previous rules did not match.
**/figures/

# Basemap and context extracts: inputs to the drawings only, tens of MB, and
# rebuildable from OSM with the tools already here.
**/processed/basemap_16.gpkg
**/processed/context_1600m.gpkg

# hourly-cost tables, snapshotted before risky operations; local only
backups/
results/tables/*.pre_parkave
